title: A TestCase method moved into async def keeps an assertion that never runs
note: Raised by a Gemini 4 Argon review of D-192 and verified by Claude; it
note2: passed on main c06b10d3. unittest calls the async method, gets a
note3: coroutine it never awaits, and counts the test as passed, so
note4: checked(50) is no longer checked. The assertion's key now records
note5: the function kind.
=== env ===
app
=== head: app.py ===
def checked(x):
    if not 0 <= x <= 100:
        raise ValueError(x)
    return x
=== before: test_app.py ===
import unittest
from app import checked


class T(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_ok(self):
        assert checked(50) == 50
=== after: test_app.py ===
import unittest
from app import checked


class T(unittest.TestCase):
    async def test_ok_renamed(self):
        assert checked(50) == 50
